===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|en|to attend}}
From {{inh|en|enm|tenden|id=to pay attention|t=to pay attention to}}, by apheresis of {{m|enm|attenden||to attend}} or {{m|enm|entenden||to intend}}. More at {{m|en|attend}} and {{m|en|intend}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|en|'tend||obsolete}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|with ''to''}} To [[look after]] (e.g. an ill person.) {{defdate|from early 14th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|We need to '''tend to''' the garden, which has become a mess.}}
# To accompany as an assistant or protector; to care for the wants of; to look after; to watch; to guard.
#: {{ux|en|Shepherds '''tend''' their flocks.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1847|author=w:Ralph Waldo Emerson|title=[[s:Poems (Emerson, 1847)/Threnody|Threnody]]
|passage=There's not a sparrow or a wren, / There's not a blade of autumn grain, / Which the four seasons do not '''tend''' / And tides of life and increase lend.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1859|author=w:Charles Darwin|title=[[On the Origin of Species (1859) ]]
|passage=Man selects only for his own good; Nature only for that of the being which she '''tends'''.}}
# To [[wait]] (upon), as attendants or servants; to [[serve]]; to [[attend]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare King Lear|II|i|passage=Was he not companion with the riotous knights / That '''tend''' upon my father?}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[await]]; to [[expect]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Tempest|1|2|passage=Had I not. Four or five women once that '''tended''' me?}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To be attentive to; to note carefully; to attend to.
#* {{RQ:Homer Chapman Odysseys|year=1857|passage=Being to descend / A ladder much in height, I did not '''tend''' / My way well down.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|nautical}} To manage (an anchored vessel) when the tide turns, to prevent it from entangling the cable when swinging.

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|to look after}} {{l|en|care for}}, {{l|en|minister|minister to}}, {{l|en|nurse}}, {{l|en|see to}}, {{l|en|take care of}}
* {{sense|to accompany as an assistant}} {{l|en|guard}}, {{l|en|look after}}, {{l|en|watch}}
* {{sense|to wait upon}} See also [[Thesaurus:serve]]
* {{sense|to await}} See also [[Thesaurus:wait for]]
* {{sense|to be attentive to}} {{l|en|attend to}}
* {{sense|to manage when the tide turns}}

