===Etymology 3===
{{etymid|en|to ignite}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*den-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|tenden|id=to ignite}}, from {{inh|en|ang|tendan||to kindle, set on fire}} (usually in compounds {{m|ang|ātendan}}, {{m|ang|fortendan}}, {{m|ang|ontendan}}), from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*tandijaną||to kindle}}, of unknown origin. Cognate with {{cog|da|tænde||to kindle}}, {{cog|sv|tända||to ignite}}, {{cog|got|𐍄𐌰𐌽𐌳𐌾𐌰𐌽||to kindle}}, {{cog|is|tendra||to ignite}}, {{cog|de|zünden||to light, ignite, fire}}. Related to {{l|en|tinder}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|en|teend|tende|tind|tine}}

